    "status": "present",
    "value": "Let k be the bit length of t, so 2^(k-1) <= t < 2^k. k accelerations travel 2^k - 1. If t = 2^k - 1, the answer is k. Otherwise there are two shapes of an optimal first run. Overshoot: k A's, then R, then solve the remaining distance 2^k - 1 - t, costing k + 1 + dp[2^k - 1 - t]. Stop short: k - 1 A's reach 2^(k-1) - 1, then R, then j A's backwards (0 <= j < k - 1) covering 2^j - 1, then R, then solve the remaining distance t - (2^(k-1) - 1) + (2^j - 1), costing (k - 1) + 1 + j + 1 + dp[...]. Take the minimum. Distances are symmetric under direction, so dp on positive distances suffices."
  },
