        "value": "R resets the speed to magnitude 1, so whatever distance is left is a fresh instance of the problem in some direction. Runs of A's cover 1, 3, 7, ..., 2^n - 1. So a path is a sequence of such runs separated by reversals, and you only need to decide the first one or two runs."
      },
