        "status": "present",
        "value": "For t from 1 to target, compute k as the bit length. If t is 2^k - 1, set dp[t] = k. Otherwise start with the overshoot cost k + 1 + dp[2^k - 1 - t], then for j from 0 to k - 2 try k + 1 + j + dp[t - (2^(k-1) - 1) + (2^j - 1)]. Both candidates use this exact loop; JavaScript computes the bit length with 32 - Math.clz32(t)."
      },
